{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_comment": "Explicit per-FFmpeg-release-line support manifest. Each release line (major.minor key) carries its OWN full list of supported builder catalog library ids (with FFmpeg's pkg-config minimum where configure pins one) and supported builder configure-option ids. NOT derived as a diff: both the supported-library set AND each minVersion are extracted by parsing that release tag's configure script (the FFmpeg Changelog/comparison docs are unreliable for both presence and minimums). Adding or auditing a release is a self-contained data edit. A library id absent from a release's 'libraries' map is unsupported by FFmpeg in that release (its --enable switch does not exist) and the planner blocks selecting it. A release line with no entry is not yet manifested; the planner skips gating and FFmpeg configure is the backstop. minVersion is set only for libraries FFmpeg version-checks via pkg-config; libraries checked by header macro (mp3lame, twolame, zvbi, x264/x265 BUILD) or with no floor carry none. Library ids match internal/planning catalog ids. Note: onnxruntime's --enable-libonnxruntime is master-only (no released version), so it is absent from every release. A library present with 'unavailable: true' has the --enable switch in that release but cannot be built because the package this builder can supply does not satisfy it (e.g. lensfun, which FFmpeg gates by the lf_db_create symbol the available lensfun package lacks); it is blocked with a 'package too old' message, distinct from an absent (FFmpeg-lacks-the-feature) library.",
